  "details": "I know I'm not the only one experiencing this, for I have seen multiple reports of the issue on several websites.  It appears Linux users like me, and thus Steam Deck users, are unable to use Selfie Expression.  Other applications can use the camera when run under Proton.\n\nI've done some research, and it looks like either...\n\n* Proton might not have enough implemented for VRChat to start the camera stream, or\n\n* VRChat isn't doing something right to get the camera stream started under Proton.\n\nThe issue also isn't specific to particular hardware, Linux distributions, or desktop environments — I've tried both my laptop's camera itself and OBS's Virtual Camera, and both KDE Plasma and GNOME, to no success.  In all cases, the camera is listed, and even though it is in a 4:3 aspect ratio as required, the same message appears — ‘Selfie Expression disabled: Webcam incompatible or in use by another app’.\n\nI'd love to see if any Linux users have managed to get Selfie Expression working — if you have, please tell how!\n\n***\n\nTechnical Information:\n\nOS:  Ubuntu 25.04\n\nKernel:  Linux 6.14.0-29-generic\n\nHost:  MSI Bravo 15in B7EDP\n\nCPU:  AMD Ryzen 7 7840HS (16 cores)\n\nGPU, Discrete:  AMD Radeon RX 6500M\n\nGPU, Integrated:  AMD Radeon 780M",
